TITLE:: SDGFxControl
summary:: insert effects played from Tidal, event by event, and their lfos on Tidal's cycle
categories:: Libraries>SuperDirtGUI
related:: Classes/SuperDirtGUI, Classes/SDGInsert, Classes/FxLfo

DESCRIPTION::
Made by link::Classes/SuperDirtGUI:: as code::~sdg.fxControl::, freed with it. An insert built on FxParamUnit that is link::Classes/SDGInsert#-listening:: has a Tidal name, which is a sound of the library while it listens. Its parameters are plain words, and code::n:: picks a preset:

code::
d9 $ s "growl*8" # drive1 (range 0 24 sine) # tone 2000 # n "<0 3>"
d1 $ s "bd*4" # fx "growl" (mix 0.5 # tone 800)
::

The sound plays nothing and leaves the orbit's other global effects alone; only the words its event carries count, never the orbit's defaults, and never SuperDirt's own (link::#*reservedWords::). On a sound event, Tidal's code::fx name:: renames the words to code::growl_mix:: and a module (code::sdgfxctl::) reads those; code::s "sdgcontrol":: reads only those too. The values go to the insert's synth in the event's own bundle, into its object without a word to its window, and into the effect's state. The window is told at most link::#*redrawRate:: times a second. The last value stays.

A name that is already a sample bank or a synth of the library is not taken over: a warning is posted, and code::fx:: still reaches the insert.

An insert whose effect uses FxLfo's clock (Growl, Tunnel, Spiral) is told Tidal's cps and cycle from every event, listening or not, when the cps changes or half a cycle after it was last told. docs/sequencing-inserts.md has the whole story and how it was measured.

CLASSMETHODS::

METHOD:: soundName
The sound that reads only prefixed words (code::growl_mix::), code::\sdgcontrol::.

METHOD:: reservedWords
SuperDirt's own event keys: never read as an effect's parameter from a sound's event.

METHOD:: plainWordsOf
An effect's plain words: each key and its lower case, but the reserved ones.
ARGUMENT:: keys

METHOD:: moduleName
The module that reads the words on sound events, code::\sdgfxctl::.

METHOD:: redrawRate
How often a second, at most, a sequenced effect's window is told of new values. 10.

METHOD:: wordsOf
code::[word, key]:: pairs for a name and its keys: each as written, and lower case when that differs.
ARGUMENT:: name
ARGUMENT:: keys

INSTANCEMETHODS::

METHOD:: sdg
Its link::Classes/SuperDirtGUI::.

METHOD:: heardWords
The prefixed words heard now (code::growl_mix::), sorted.

METHOD:: soundNames
The insert names that are sounds of the library now.

METHOD:: isLibrarySound
Whether the library has the name as a bank or a synth that is not one of these.
ARGUMENT:: name

METHOD:: dispatchSound
What an event of an insert's sound says to it, and the clock. Called inside the event's bundle.
ARGUMENT:: name
ARGUMENT:: event

METHOD:: library
SuperDirt's sound library.

METHOD:: dirt
The SuperDirt.

METHOD:: rebuild
The words and the clocked inserts read again from the inserts. Happens on its own on every change of them.

METHOD:: dispatch
What an event's prefixed words say to the inserts, and the clock. Called inside the event's bundle.
ARGUMENT:: event

METHOD:: isWanted
Whether anything listens or wants the clock: the module's test.

METHOD:: freeName
A name an insert of a kind can have: the kind, else kind2, kind3 ...
ARGUMENT:: kind
ARGUMENT:: except
the insert asking, whose own name does not count.

METHOD:: isTaken
Whether another insert has the name.
ARGUMENT:: name
ARGUMENT:: except

METHOD:: nameProblem
What is wrong with a name for an insert, or nil.
ARGUMENT:: name
ARGUMENT:: insert

METHOD:: free
The sounds and the module out.
